1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,397
For the second in our series about locally-run businesses,

2
00:00:04,397 --> 00:00:10,260
we meet Simon Winridge, co-founder of the hugely-successful Winridge Forest Railway Park.

3
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:16,630
Welcome, Simon. Now, perhaps you can begin by telling us a little bit about how it all started.

4
00:00:16,630 --> 00:00:19,175
Well, during the 1970s, my wife,

5
00:00:19,175 --> 00:00:24,440
Liz and I had just acquired 80 acres of sheep-farming land

6
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:27,660
and we decided to settle down and have children.

7
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:31,800
Pretty soon we had a daughter, Sarah, and a son, Duncan.

8
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:35,058
The place was wonderful for the kids:

9
00:00:35,058 --> 00:00:42,040
they particularly loved trains and gradually built up an enormous network of miniature railway track.

10
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:44,728
I began to develop larger-scale models of locomotives

11
00:00:44,728 --> 00:00:51,446
but we didn't think anything more of it until I went on a trip to a theme park near Birmingham

12
00:00:51,446 --> 00:00:54,470
and decided we could do a much better job!

13
00:00:54,470 --> 00:00:59,664
So we set up a small one ourselves based on the miniature railway

14
00:00:59,664 --> 00:01:04,458
and we opened to the public for just a month that year,

15
00:01:04,458 --> 00:01:11,650
1984-in July-our driest month-because our children said they didn't want our guests to have a miserable, wet visit.

16
00:01:11,650 --> 00:01:16,910
I dealt with Park business and Liz carried on with the farm work.

17
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:21,510
It soon became clear that we were onto a winner.

18
00:01:21,510 --> 00:01:24,440
We began to extend the railway track

19
00:01:24,440 --> 00:01:28,752
and lay it among more interesting landscape by planting trees,

20
00:01:28,752 --> 00:01:34,290
which in turn attracted more wildlife, and by making cuttings through the rock.

21
00:01:34,290 --> 00:01:36,458
Nowadays, we're open all year round

22
00:01:36,458 --> 00:01:44,770
and we're pleased to say that Winridge is one of the most popular visitor attractions in the area-with 50,000 visitors a year -

23
00:01:44,770 --> 00:01:49,830
a million and a half people have been through our doors since we opened.

24
00:01:49,830 --> 00:01:54,120
All these visitors mean we have had to expand our operation

25
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:57,620
and it's now a truly family concern.

26
00:01:57,620 --> 00:01:59,450
I'm near to retirement age

27
00:01:59,450 --> 00:02:05,670
so I only concern myself with looking after the mechanical side of things - keeping the trains going.

28
00:02:05,670 --> 00:02:09,320
Liz now devotes all her energies to recruiting

29
00:02:09,320 --> 00:02:11,763
and supporting the large squadron of workers,

30
00:02:11,763 --> 00:02:14,200
which keep the place running smoothly.

31
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:18,420
We're really pleased that after some years away teaching

32
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:19,539
Sarah has now returned to the park

33
00:02:19,539 --> 00:02:24,060
and makes sure the visitors are kept fed and watered

34
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:25,880
which keeps her pretty busy as you can imagine.

35
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:30,815
Our son, Duncan, has been a stalwart of the park for the last ten years,

36
00:02:30,815 --> 00:02:33,980
taking over from me in the area of construction

37
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:37,724
and I'll say a little bit more about that in a moment -

38
00:02:37,724 --> 00:02:42,330
and his new wife, Judith, has also joined the team in charge of retail.

39
00:02:42,330 --> 00:02:48,330
That's becoming a tremendous growth area for us-a lot of people want to buy souvenirs.

40
00:02:48,330 --> 00:02:51,920
So have you finished your development of the site for the moment?

41
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:56,630
Not at all! We've constantly looking for ways to offer more to our visitors.

42
00:02:56,630 --> 00:02:58,967
The railway remains the central feature

43
00:02:58,967 --> 00:03:05,200
and there's now 1.2 kilometres of the line laid but we'd like to lay more.

44
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:10,280
Because of the geology of the area, our greatest problem is digging tunnels.

45
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:12,600
But we're gradually overcoming that.

46
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:17,100
We're also very pleased with a new installation of the GO-Kart arena

47
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:20,000
which is 120 square metres in area.

48
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,980
Again the problem is the geology

49
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:26,800
we had to level the mounds on the track for safety reasons.

50
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:34,700
We wanted to enable 5-12 year olds to use the go-karts. And the main attraction here is the Formula 1 Kart.

51
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:38,564
We've known fights to break out over who gets it!

52
00:03:38,564 --> 00:03:43,200
And then finally to our most recent development which is the landscaped...
